# Architecture

Three packages, one rule each.

- `internal/ledger` — append-only double entry. Balances are folds, never
  stored. This is deliberate: a stored balance is a second source of truth and
  every reconciliation bug we had in the previous system came from one.
- `internal/risk` — pure scoring. No IO, no clock. Testable in isolation.
- `internal/gateway` — HTTP translation only. It must hold no business rule;
  if a rule appears here it belongs in ledger or risk.

## Why payments are held, not rejected

A score at or above `risk.Threshold` returns 202, not 4xx. A held payment is a
queue entry a human resolves; a rejection is final and loses the customer.
